  "markdown": "|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Search JOS Website | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| JOS Home Page | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| JOS Online Publications | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Index of terms in JOS Website | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Index: Introduction to Digital Filters with Audio Applications | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Introduction to Digital Filters with Audio Applications | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| The Simplest Lowpass Filter | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| The Simplest Lowpass Filter | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| What is a Filter? | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Click for https://ccrma.stanford.edu/CCRMA/Courses/152/hearing.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Click for https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pasp/Ideal\\_Vibrating\\_String.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| A signal is typically a real-valued function of time. A discrete-time signal is typically a real-valued function of discrete time, and is therefore a time-ordered sequence of real numbers. \u00a0\u2014\u00a0 Click for http://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Definition\\_Signal.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Click for https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pasp/Parallel\\_Body\\_Filterbank\\_Design.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Click for http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/java/elements/elements.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Click for http://www.circuitsage.com/filter.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| A _filter_ in the audio signal processing context is any operation that accepts a signal as an input and produces a signal as an output. Most practical audio filters are _linear_ and _time invariant_, in which case they can be characterized by their _impulse response_ or their _frequency response_. \u00a0\u2014\u00a0 Click for https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/What\\_Filter.html | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Search JOS Website | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| JOS Home Page | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| JOS Online Publications | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Index of terms in JOS Website | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Index: Introduction to Digital Filters with Audio Applications | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| Introduction to Digital Filters with Audio Applications | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| The Simplest Lowpass Filter | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| The Simplest Lowpass Filter | |\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| What is a Filter? | |\n\n **[Next](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/What_Filter.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Prev](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Simplest_Lowpass_Filter.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Up](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Simplest_Lowpass_Filter.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Top](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/%7Ejos/filters/filters.html)**\n**\\|**\n**[Index](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Index_this_Document.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[JOS Index](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/GlobalJOSIndex.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[JOS Pubs](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pubs.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[JOS Home](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/%7Ejos) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Search](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/index.html#searchform)**\n\n* * *\n\n## Introduction\n\nMusicians have been using [filters](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/What_Filter.html) for thousands of years to shape the\nsounds of their art in various ways. For example, the evolution of the\nphysical dimensions of the violin constitutes an evolution in [filter\\\\\ndesign](http://www.circuitsage.com/filter.html). The choice of wood, the shape of the cutouts, the [geometry](http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/java/elements/elements.html) of\nthe bridge, and everything that affects resonance all have a bearing\non how the violin [body filters](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pasp/Parallel_Body_Filterbank_Design.html) the [signal](http://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Definition_Signal.html) induced at the bridge by the\n[vibrating strings](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pasp/Ideal_Vibrating_String.html). Once a sound is airborne there is yet more\nfiltering performed by the listening environment, by the pinnae of the\near, and by idiosyncrasies of the [hearing](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/CCRMA/Courses/152/hearing.html) process.\n\n* * *\n\n**Subsections**\n\n- [What is a Filter?](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/What_Filter.html)\n- [Why learn about filters?](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Why_learn_about_filters.html)\n\n* * *\n\n**[Next](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/What_Filter.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Prev](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Simplest_Lowpass_Filter.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Up](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Simplest_Lowpass_Filter.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Top](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/%7Ejos/filters/filters.html)**\n**\\|**\n**[Index](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/Index_this_Document.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[JOS Index](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/GlobalJOSIndex.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[JOS Pubs](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pubs.html) \u00a0\\|**\n**[JOS Home](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/%7Ejos) \u00a0\\|**\n**[Search](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/index.html#searchform)**\n\n* * *\n\n[\\[How to cite this work\\]](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/filters-citation.html) [\\[Order a printed hardcopy\\]](https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/filters/filters-hardcopy.html) [\\[Comment on this page via email\\]](mailto:jos@ccrma.stanford.edu?subject=Introduction%20to%20Digital%20Filters%20with%20Audio%20Applications&body=[Please%20paste%20the%20page%20URL%20here%20and%20then%20comment.])\n\n* * *\n\n##### \\`\\` [Introduction to Digital Filters with Audio Applications](htt